a dock that's a projector for your  Nintendo switch sounds like a sweet idea  right  well the crowdfunded Ojo projector is  exactly that and we had some hands-on  time with a feature complete prototype  thanks to the creators yes Oh Joe and we  have some thoughts on what it does right  and where it can be better  [Music]  first question to address is how good is  the actual projector  well the Oh Joe uses DMD LED tech from  Texas Instruments which provides 200  lumens of brightness from our experience  this isn't all that bright unless the  room you're in is quite dark it'd be  hard to figure out exactly what's going  on in game especially if the game  environment is dark the front of the  projectors pulled back the dimmer the  image will be just by nature of  dispersing the concentration of light  it's said to be able to project between  30 inches and 120 inches of screen space  at about 3 feet away  I had a roughly 30 inch image with  decent brightness pulling it back to  around 10 feet gave me a much bigger  image but things got a little hazy it's  also fairly low res at 854 by 480 a 16  by 9 aspect ratio games are certainly  playable at this resolution but details  are hard to make out in certain games  the text and zelda breath of the wild  was a bit tough to read and at night the  world is tough to navigate but under the  right conditions the projector can look  just fine if you're not too concerned  with visual fidelity I suppose it's  intended for more party oriented games  seeing as how the Ojo isn't ideal for  games that require more attention to  detail like Zelda though Jo has a ton of  bells and whistles though it's  battery-powered so it doesn't need to be  plugged in to use it charges through USB  C and can even use the normal switch  dock plug the projector itself can last  up to 5 hours on a full charge and can  even be set in a charge mode which will  juice up your switches battery about 3  times over with its hdmi in port you can  even use other devices if you wish you  also got two USB 3.0 ports and a 3.5  millimeter aux connection to use  headphones or other external audio  devices if not the ojos 5 watt speaker  can be pretty loud and sounds decent  despite coming out of a small device its  cooling system seemed to keep the switch  and the projector quite cool and didn't  get very loud  the Ojo projector is a neat idea with  plenty of well-thought-out features to  complement it but at its core it  displays switch games at a larger format  which is where it comes up a bit short  with the brighter screen and sharper  resolution it could really shine  but for now you'd have to find the right  conditions to be able to use it  optimally mojo projector made his  crowdfunding goal in IndieGoGo last  month and early bird packs are still  available for 300 bucks units our plan  to ship out in December  stick the game spot for coverage on  switch games accessories and news since  we have plenty more on the way thanks  for watching
 

